+// THE DEPLOY-ARTIFACT-CLOSURE GATE, wired ONCE over the realized apply plan (refuse-only): the
+// sanctioned follow-up named in gunbc.live_deploy.deploy_artifact_read_sets. If an artifact a deployed
+// unit READS is not WRITTEN by some install leg, the whole plan is refused BEFORE any enable leg runs
+// (red_control 2). Reads come from the roster read-sets (deployment_artifact_read_rows over
+// deployment_owned_steps); owned comes from the LEG destinations. Proceed returns the plan UNCHANGED
+// (zero legs added); only a Halt adds a refusal -- the gate never widens the plan (refuse-only).
+// A converger's kind, taken from its unit's OWN [Service] Type=. Which leg counts as "the plan RUNS the
+// converger" is decided by this kind as a TOTAL match -- not "either leg will do for both".
+// A oneshot converger (e.g. tree-remote, a typed oneshot -- #16544) RUNS during the deploy; a long-running
+// converger is brought up by being ENABLED (starts and stays up).
+type ConvergerUnitKind =
+  | Oneshot
+  | LongRunning
+
+fn leg_step_present(legs: List<DeployApplyLeg>, step: String) -> Bool {
+  match first_where(xs: legs, keep: fn(l) { deploy_apply_leg_step(l) == step }) {
+    Present { value: _ } => true
+    Absent => false
+  }
